course: dictionary
lesson: 13192
title: Fruity and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Fruity is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a fruity drink or a fruity smell. Its main meaning is about taste and smell. «The lemonade was sweet and fruity, with a sharp tang.» The words sweet and tang tell you it tastes strongly of fruit.
explain: Fruity can also describe a voice. «Grandad gave a fruity laugh that filled the whole kitchen.» A fruity voice is deep, rich and warm. It does not taste of anything. Ask yourself: is the sentence about food and smell, or about sound?
explain: In informal speech, fruity can mean a bit cheeky or rude. «The comedian told a fruity joke, and the teacher went red.» Check the meaning by putting it into the sentence: does a cheeky joke fit? It does. Some old slang uses of this word are unkind, so never use them.
fact: Fruity means tasting or smelling strongly of fruit.
fact: A fruity voice is deep, rich and warm.
fact: In informal British English, «fruity» can mean a bit cheeky or rude, as in «a fruity joke».
fact: Fruity is an adjective, so it can change to «fruitier» and «fruitiest».
fact: Some old slang uses of this word are unkind, so do not use them.
exercise: «The orange juice had a fruity flavour, sweet and sharp.» What does fruity mean here? | Very loud | Made of wood | *Tasting strongly of fruit | Cold and icy
exercise: «Grandad gave a fruity laugh that filled the kitchen.» What kind of sound is a fruity laugh? | Thin and high | *Deep, rich and warm | Quiet and shy | Broken
exercise: «The comedian told a fruity joke that made the teacher blush.» What does fruity mean here? | *A bit cheeky or rude | Wet and muddy | Slow and sleepy | Sour like a lemon
test: «The candles had a fruity smell of apples and cherries.» Which words tell you fruity is about smell? | candles | *apples and cherries | the candles had | had
test: Which is the correct form to compare two things, as in «this juice is ___ than that one»? | fruitiest | fruitness | *fruitier | fruit
exam: Jayden says, «The fruity pie was lovely.» What is the best meaning here? | Made of stone | Very cold and hard | *Tasting strongly of fruit | Angry and loud
